waivers:
  - finding: "HarHeader, HarQueryParam and HarCookie are three structurally identical {name, value} structs"
    reason: "Kept distinct because HAR 1.2 gives the three list-element types different optional fields - cookies carry expires/httpOnly/path/domain/secure, which har.rs's own doc comment already records as deliberately unparsed for now, so HarCookie is the one expected to grow them. Collapsing now would have to be un-collapsed then, and the three belong to one wire format that must be free to diverge from the REST view's HeaderView independently."
  - finding: "encode_body allocates an owned String per captured body rather than writing incrementally into the output buffer"
    reason: "Unavoidable inside serde's derive-based data model - the value must exist before serde walks the tree, and true incremental output would need a hand-written streaming Serialize. An export is a user-triggered one-shot download, not a hot path, so this falls under the rubric's exclusion of micro-optimization outside hot paths. The peak-memory consequence is separately recorded as the epic's deferred streaming-export row, now quantified at roughly 4x the ring cap."
verdict: PASS
